ne tension which avoids overshoot / undershoot artefacts. The most visible improvements are in accuracy of derivatives at points along the boundary and extrapolation of data beyond the boundary of a mesh.","position":{"start":{"line":28,"column":1},"end":{"line":28,"column":1}},"key":"PVYqX8uGjJ"}],"key":"QwHisaLrfx"},{"type":"container","kind":"figure","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/underworldcode.org-preview/3b77403c0d/build/spline_tension-aa273ee3f70d325fe22f7cc53a019e38.png","alt":"Difference between derivatives evaluated at the poles with spline tension vs. without. Looks like a beautiful flower. (Graphic generated with LavaVu).","data":{"altTextIsAutoGenerated":true},"key":"xdwTilMkOW","urlSource":"figures/spline_tension.png"},{"type":"caption","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":32,"column":1},"end":{"line":32,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Difference between derivatives evaluated at the poles with spline tension vs. without. Looks like a beautiful flower. (Graphic generated with LavaVu).","position":{"start":{"line":32,"column":1},"end":{"line":32,"column":1}},"key":"fdmVnpqFJl"}],"key":"Z6xAlyjwIz"}],"key":"DIxmR1d0iI"}],"enumerator":"2","key":"JFRRhkBRuN"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Voronoi diagram","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"key":"UFtZpT5ZUG"}],"key":"ysKezo2OdW"},{"type":"text","value":" - the Voronoi diagram is the dual of a Delaunay triangulation. For every triangle in the mesh, there is a voronoi point which lies at an equal radius from each node. The diagram is constructed by connecting up the voronoi points from each neighbouring triangle.","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"key":"V0Ss4AUMxX"}],"key":"wIIYcBSdc4"},{"ty